    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278">

                <pb facs="0431" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/254: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-11-14T14:00:00+00:00">November 14,
                            1934—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 14—11:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. Supplementing my 31, November 13, 9 p.m., I told Simon I was inclined to
                    believe that if there were to be a pact of non-aggression for the Pacific and
                    the Far East we would come to the conclusion, in examining the matter, that if
                    it were limited to the United States, England and Japan, it would create
                    suspicion and resentment on the part of other powers interested in the Far East
                    and that in my personal opinion if there is to be a proper basis for a pact of
                    non-aggression, all of the signatures to the Nine-Power Treaty<anchor n="71"
                        xml:id="d278-f1"/> and also Russia should be included. He replied that he
                    had not thought of that but that it was a most interesting and excellent
                    suggestion to which his first impression was favorable. We both agreed that the
                    crux of such a problem would depend upon the extent to which Japan would bind
                    herself not to pursue a policy that would provoke aggression.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
